  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSOLIDATING SEA TURTLE CONSERVATION IN THE AZORES 5 (COSTA5)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to collaborate with long line fisherman and the Azores Regional Directorate of Marine Affairs to minimize the impacts of fisheries bycatch on the large juvenile loggerhead foraging population in in the Azores. Activities include: 1) placing two observers on LL fishing vessels for 12 months to collect additional bycatch data; 2) analyzing these data and previously collected bycatch data to identify critical interaction zones; 3) restructure the turtle tagging activities in cooperation with local partners and expand tagging program with new partners; and 4) promote best practices for safe handling and release of accidentally captured turtles by LL fisherman through training workshops and brochures.</narrative>
  </description>
